W44-78 widen-W44-29-gate A/B sweep — 2026-05-19
================================================

Goal
----
Test candidate widenings of the W44-29 auto-fire gate
(`HIGH_D_PHOTO_MIN_DISTANCE = 4.0` AND `HIGH_D_PHOTO_SMOOTH_THRESHOLD = 50.0`)
after the W44-77 sweep found that simply forcing the
`EntropyMulTable::high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed` table on cells outside
the current gate saved up to 1705 B per cell.

Variants tested
---------------
  default (no widening):  distance >= 4.0 AND mask1x1_median < 50.0   (current production)
  A (dist>=3):            distance >= 3.0 AND mask1x1_median < 50.0   (lower distance gate)
  B (mask<80):            distance >= 4.0 AND mask1x1_median < 80.0   (lift mask gate)
  C (dist>=3 mask<80):    distance >= 3.0 AND mask1x1_median < 80.0   (both lifts)
  D (dist>=2.5 mask<95):  distance >= 2.5 AND mask1x1_median < 95.0   (most aggressive)

Method
------
- 46 images total: all 41 CID22-512 validation photos + 5 gb82-sc screenshots
  (codec_wiki, imac_g3, terminal, windows95, graph).
- 5 distances per image: 2.5, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0, 6.0.
- effort=7, threads=8, butteraugli loop OFF (e7 default).
- Each (image, distance) cell encoded once per variant. When a variant's
  gate decision matches default, the encode is reused (no duplicate work).
- `mask1x1_median` is the encoder-internal value from
  `examples/w44_65_encoder_mask1x1_probe.rs`.
- cjxl reference: libjxl v0.12 HEAD at
  `/home/lilith/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl/build/tools/cjxl`, `-d <d> -e 7`.

Cell flips ("FIXED" = bytes within 1.5 % of cjxl, matching cjxl_parity_ledger)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Variant                   Δbytes(B)  FIXED→OPEN  OPEN→FIXED
default (no widening)            0          0           0
A (dist>=3 mask<50)          -2564          0           1   ← clean win
B (mask<80)                   +919          7           7
C (dist>=3 mask<80)          -3604          9          10
D (dist>=2.5 mask<95)        -5713         11          14

Variant A is the only widening that closes cells without ANY
`FIXED → OPEN` regression.

