Hash-lock impact (verified via `examples/w44_78_gradient_mask_probe.rs`)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
- `lossy_distance_3` fixture (32×32 gradient @ d=3.0):
  mask1x1_median = 96.74 → does NOT trigger widened gate
  (96.74 > 50.0 mask threshold). Hash byte-identical.
- All `lossy_*_48x48_noise` fixtures encode at d=1.0:
  1.0 < 3.0 widened distance gate → does NOT trigger. Hash byte-identical.
- All other lossy hash-locks encode at d <= 1.0: same — no trigger.
- Predicted hash-lock regen count: 0.

Reproducer
----------
cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder --features parallel \
    --example w44_78_widen_gate_ab

Host: water-cooled 7950X, 128 GB RAM, Linux 6.6.114.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2.
Git: branch main (W44-77 commits e18e94d4 + 1ea61f79 in tree).

Recommendation
--------------
Ship `HIGH_D_PHOTO_MIN_DISTANCE: 4.0 → 3.0` (one-line constant change in
`jxl-encoder/src/vardct/encoder.rs`). No widening of
`HIGH_D_PHOTO_SMOOTH_THRESHOLD` (keep at 50.0). Zero hash-lock
regen. Expected RD-pareto ledger movement: +1 FIXED (1420710.png e7
d=3) ± any e5/e6/e8/e9 cells the d=3 distance gate now touches
(separately measured via cjxl_parity_ledger refresh post-ship).
